WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.394
If an acquisition has to state
a FIPS 140-3 expectation,

2
00:00:04.394 --> 00:00:07.000
the honest answer has two halves.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.921
The control components are in good shape:

4
00:00:09.921 --> 00:00:15.246
FIPS mode is on by default on recent
releases and in the hosted environment,

5
00:00:15.246 --> 00:00:20.400
and Cisco's letter for the current
train cites an active FIPS 140-3 module.

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.763
The edges are different.

7
00:00:21.763 --> 00:00:24.861
Cisco's current letters
don't name SD-WAN mode,

8
00:00:24.861 --> 00:00:29.049
and Cisco's own example shows an
edge with FIPS mode disabled.

9
00:00:29.049 --> 00:00:34.325
So get edge validation in SD-WAN mode as
a written vendor commitment before award.

10
00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:38.708
For edge hardening, the agency sets
its own baseline from the Center

11
00:00:38.708 --> 00:00:43.325
for Internet Security benchmark for
IOS XE and Cisco's hardening guide.

12
00:00:43.325 --> 00:00:47.575
The router STIGs are Defense material,
an optional cross-check at most.

13
00:00:47.575 --> 00:00:49.490
Next, TIC 3.0.
